{
  "$comment": [
    "reflux's profile over accrete's vocabulary: selection, defaults, and the class-token vocabulary.",
    "It holds NO type definitions — the types come from schema/accrete.schema.json and nowhere else.",
    "Read by tools/gen_sdk.py (builders + gates) and, at runtime, by reflux/sdk/profile.py.",
    "",
    "positional:  what the first positional argument of ui.<type>() means — `children` (the child nodes)",
    "             or `value` (a static value: the display/data payload the renderer reads). null = none.",
    "children:    the builder takes *children.  item: the builder takes item= (the wire's `item` template).",
    "bind:        per bind key, which kinds the builder offers. The shape comes from accrete's `bind` map;",
    "             this list is what the renderer actually reads/writes for that type (verified in ui_leptos).",
    "tokens:      enum value -> class token, filled in when the styling layer lands (M1). Until then the",
    "             builders offer no class strings at all — the producer cannot reach a free class."
  ],
  "hidden_attrs": [
    "class",
    "selector"
  ],
  "kwarg_renames": {
    "type": "kind"
  },
  "tokens": {
    "text": {
      "heading-1": "rx-heading-1",
      "heading-2": "rx-heading-2",
      "heading-3": "rx-heading-3",
      "code": "rx-code",
      "muted": "rx-muted",
      "danger": "rx-danger"
    },
    "case": {
      "card": "rx-card"
    }
  },
  "types": {
    "case": {
      "expose": true,
      "positional": "children",
      "children": true,
      "item": false,
      "bind": {}
    },
    "placeholder": {
      "expose": true,
      "positional": "children",
      "children": true,
      "item": false,
      "bind": {
        "value": [
          "source"
        ]
      }
    },
    "chart": {
      "expose": true,
      "positional": "value",
      "children": false,
      "item": false,
      "bind": {
        "value": [
          "default",
          "source"
        ]
      }
    },
    "diagram": {
      "expose": true,
